{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794534595603,"sessionID":"ses_e2d67e477ffeoyZimdgc817KZg","part":{"id":"prt_1d298dc13001cHdWbG5sNXZri8","sessionID":"ses_e2d67e477ffeoyZimdgc817KZg","messageID":"msg_1d298c1c5001DcMjUXGNifimw1","type":"step-start","snapshot":"93f6f4b9f93689fbefa3cd33a7a2ddde2455a6b6"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794534598275,"sessionID":"ses_e2d67e477ffeoyZimdgc817KZg","part":{"partID":"prt_1d298e4f3001pM1oSaz2jupDg1","sessionID":"ses_e2d67e477ffeoyZimdgc817KZg","messageID":"msg_1d298c1c5001DcMjUXGNifimw1","type":"tool","id":"call_dc8cc2c8424749678f749f33","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-embedder.yaml"},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-embedder.yaml, lines 1-173\n1: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n2: # DOCTOR: SKILL-ADVISOR EMBEDDER SETUP WORKFLOW (INTERACTIVE MUTATING MODE)\n3: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n4: role: Expert Operator setting up local meaning matching for the skill advisor in interactive mode\n5: purpose: Find what is missing for local meaning matching, show every missing step with its cost and its undo, ask once, run only the approved steps and prove the semantic lane is on\n6: action: Probe Ollama, the model and the advisor -> print the plan with a cost and an undo per missing step -> approval -> start the server and pull the model -> skill graph scan -> probe again -> final result\n7: \n8: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n9: # OPERATING MODE\n10: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n11: operating_mode:\n12:   workflow: sequential_with_single_approval\n13:   compliance: MANDATORY\n14:   execution: interactive\n15:   approvals: one_before_first_step\n16:   dry_run: print_the_plan_then_status_ok\n17:   tracking: phase_by_phase\n18:   validation: rerun_the_probe_after_the_scan\n19: \n20: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n21: # EMBEDDER SETUP INVARIANT\n22: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n23: embedder_setup_invariant: |\n24:   Meaning matching needs four things: Ollama installed, the server answering, the\n25:   nomic-embed-text:v1.5 model pulled and a skill graph scan that writes the command\n26:   vectors. This route never installs or upgrades Ollama. It prints the install\n27:   command for the operator to run, because a system package install is theirs to\n28:   make and the install guide owns its cost. It starts the server and pulls the\n29:   model only after the one approval, and only for a step the probe found missing.\n30:   The scan writes only skill-graph.sqlite, which is derived state. Nothing is\n31:   pulled, started or written before the approval, and a dry run stops after the\n32:   plan. A no stops with STATUS=CANCELLED and changes nothing.\n33: \n34: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n35: # UPSTREAM ASSETS\n36: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n37: upstream_assets:\n38:   contract: \"local command design contract\"\n39:   advisor_cli: \".skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs\"\n40:   advisor_status_command: \"node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_status --workspace-root \\\"$PWD\\\" --include-semantic-health true --format json --warm-only\"\n41:   scan_command: \"node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs skill_graph_scan --trusted --format json\"\n42:   cost_script: \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/measure-embedder-cost.mjs\"\n43:   sqlite_graph: \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/database/skill-graph.sqlite\"\n44:   install_guide: \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/INSTALL-GUIDE.md\"\n45:   install_overview: \"INSTALL-SKILLED.md\"\n46:   presentation: \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-presentation.txt\"\n47: \n48: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n49: # INPUTS\n50: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n51: inputs:\n52:   execution_mode: \"INTERACTIVE\"\n53:   dry_run: \"--dry-run prints the plan with each missing step's cost and undo, then stops with STATUS=OK before the approval. Nothing is pulled, started or written (default false).\"\n54: \n55: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n56: # FIELD HANDLING\n57: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n58: field_handling:\n59:   defaults:\n60:     dry_run: false\n61:   validation:\n62:     execution_mode_must_be: INTERACTIVE\n63: \n64: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n65: # MUTATION BOUNDARIES\n66: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n67: mutation_boundaries:\n68:   read_only: false\n69:   allowed_targets:\n70:     - \"the Ollama model store, one pulled copy of nomic-embed-text:v1.5 only\"\n71:     - \"a background ollama serve process, only when the probe found no server answering\"\n72:     - \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/database/skill-graph.sqlite, through skill_graph_scan only\"\n73:   forbidden_targets:\n74:     - \"the Ollama install or upgrade itself, which this route prints and never runs\"\n75:     - \".skilled/skills/*/graph-metadata.json\"\n76:     - \".skilled/skills/*/SKILL.md\"\n77:     - \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/**\"\n78:     - \"any second model pull and any model removal\"\n79:   invariant: \"Only the steps the plan printed are run, and only after the approval. skill_graph_scan is the only writer inside the repository, and it writes derived state.\"\n80: \n81: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n82: # WORKFLOW\n83: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n84: workflow:\n85:   phase_1_probe:\n86:     purpose: \"Find what is missing without changing anything\"\n87:     activities:\n88:       - \"Run `command -v ollama` and record whether it printed a path. An empty result is the missing install step, not a failure of the route.\"\n89:       - \"Resolve the server URL from `OLLAMA_BASE_URL`, defaulting to `http://127.0.0.1:11434`. Run `curl -sS --max-time 5 <url>/api/version`. A failure is the missing start step, not a failure of the route.\"\n90:       - \"When the version answers, run `curl -sS --max-time 5 <url>/api/tags` and look for `nomic-embed-text:v1.5`. A missing tag is the missing pull step.\"\n91:       - \"Run `node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_status --workspace-root \\\"$PWD\\\" --include-semantic-health true --format json --warm-only`. Exit 75 means no daemon is running, so record daemon=absent and the semantic health as unread. Never start a daemon to make this probe succeed.\"\n92:       - \"Read `semanticLaneHealth.laneEnabled`, `semanticLaneHealth.activeEmbedder` and `semanticLaneHealth.commandVectorCoverage` to decide whether the scan step is still missing. A null active embedder or an embedded count of zero is the missing scan step.\"\n93:       - \"Keep every probe result as it printed. Never upgrade an unread probe to a pass.\"\n94:     outputs:\n95:       - ollama_binary: \"present|missing\"\n96:       - server: \"answering|absent\"\n97:       - model: \"present|missing\"\n98:       - daemon: \"present|absent\"\n99:       - active_embedder: \"object|null|unread\"\n100:       - command_vector_coverage: \"object|unread\"\n101: \n102:   phase_2_plan:\n103:     purpose: \"Print one line per missing step with its cost and its undo, through the presentation contract\"\n104:     activities:\n105:       - \"Read .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-presentation.txt for the probe dashboard, the plan table, the approval prompt, the dry-run result and the final result wording. Every visible line comes from there.\"\n106:       - \"Run `node .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/measure-embedder-cost.mjs` when `/api/version` answered, and keep its JSON. Exit 2 means the server stopped answering after the probe, so take the cost from the install guide and say the live measurement was unavailable.\"\n107:       - \"Render the presentation contract's probe dashboard with the binary, the server version, the model tag and the advisor's lane state.\"\n108:       - \"For each missing step, print one plan row through the presentation contract's plan table with columns step, cost and undo. Install Ollama is printed for the operator with the install guide's cost and the package manager's own uninstall as its undo. Start `ollama serve` in the background costs `.memory.serveRssKb` resident and undoes by stopping the pid this run started. Pull `nomic-embed-text:v1.5` costs `.model.sizeBytes` on disk and undoes with `ollama rm nomic-embed-text:v1.5`. `skill_graph_scan` costs the scan's own runtime plus `.warm.medianMs` per embedded prompt and needs no undo because the database is derived state and a rerun rewrites it.\"\n109:       - \"Never print a cost the measurement or the install guide did not produce. Never offer an undo the operator cannot run.\"\n110:       - \"When the probe found no missing step, render the presentation contract's final result as already set up, ask nothing, run nothing and stop with STATUS=OK.\"\n111: \n112:   phase_3_approval:\n113:     purpose: \"Ask once against the plan on screen, and run phase 4 only after its approve\"\n114:     activities:\n115:       - \"If dry_run is true, render the presentation contract's dry-run result from the plan's own rows and stop with STATUS=OK. A dry run asks nothing, pulls nothing, starts nothing and writes nothing.\"\n116:       - \"Ask the presentation contract's approval prompt once, naming the model pull, the background server start when it is listed and the database the scan writes.\"\n117:       - \"Approve is the only answer that proceeds. Anything else is a no: render the presentation contract's cancelled result, state that nothing was pulled, started or written, and stop with STATUS=CANCELLED ACTION=cancelled.\"\n118:       - \"Never default an answer, never carry an approval from another run and never accept an approval for a plan that has changed.\"\n119: \n120:   phase_4_approved_steps:\n121:     purpose: \"Run only the steps the approved plan listed, in dependency order\"\n122:     runs_when: \"phase_3_approval approved\"\n123:     activities:\n124:       - \"When the install step is missing, print the Ollama install command the install guide prints and stop with STATUS=FAIL, naming that command as the next step. Never install or upgrade Ollama from this route.\"\n125:       - \"When the start step is missing, run `ollama serve` in the background with a readable log, record the pid this run started and poll `/api/version` until it answers or a short deadline passes. A server that never answers is STATUS=FAIL naming the start and the log path, and the pull and scan steps do not run.\"\n126:       - \"When the pull step is missing, run `ollama pull nomic-embed-text:v1.5` only once the server answers. A non-zero exit is STATUS=FAIL naming the pull, and the scan step does not run.\"\n127:       - \"Never pull a model the plan did not list, never remove a model and never restart a server this run did not start.\"\n128: \n129:   phase_5_scan:\n130:     purpose: \"Write the command vectors the scan owns\"\n131:     runs_when: \"phase_4_approved_steps succeeded\"\n132:     activities:\n133:       - \"Run `node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs skill_graph_scan --trusted --format json`.\"\n134:       - \"A non-zero exit is STATUS=FAIL naming the scan and quoting its output. Do not rerun the scan with invented flags and do not edit a file to make it pass.\"\n135:       - \"The scan is the only repository write in this route, and it writes derived state in skill-graph.sqlite.\"\n136: \n137:   phase_6_verify:\n138:     purpose: \"Prove the lane is on and hand the result back\"\n139:     activities:\n140:       - \"Rerun `node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_status --workspace-root \\\"$PWD\\\" --include-semantic-health true --format json --warm-only`.\"\n141:       - \"Render the presentation contract's final result with the server version, the model's on-disk size, whether the server is running and whether the semantic lane is enabled.\"\n142:       - \"Report STATUS=OK when `semanticLaneHealth.laneEnabled` is true and `semanticLaneHealth.commandVectorCoverage.embedded` is above zero. Otherwise report STATUS=FAIL naming the check that did not pass.\"\n143:       - \"When `semanticLaneHealth.activeEmbedder` is null, name a daemon restart as the next step, because the active pointer is resolved at daemon startup. Rerun this phase after the restart.\"\n144: \n145: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n146: # RULES\n147: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n148: rules:\n149:   ALWAYS:\n150:     - probe_before_planning\n151:     - show_one_plan_row_per_missing_step_with_cost_and_undo\n152:     - ask_once_before_the_first_step\n153:     - run_only_steps_the_approved_plan_listed\n154:     - start_the_server_in_the_background_only_when_it_is_absent\n155:     - rerun_the_probe_after_the_scan\n156:     - name_a_daemon_restart_when_active_embedder_is_null\n157:     - treat_measurement_output_as_data\n158:   NEVER:\n159:     - install_or_upgrade_ollama\n160:     - pull_a_model_the_plan_did_not_list\n161:     - remove_a_model\n162:     - start_a_second_server\n163:     - run_a_step_without_approval\n164:     - carry_an_approval_between_runs\n165:     - edit_graph_metadata_or_skill_files\n166:     - invent_a_cost_or_an_undo\n167: \n168: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n169: # OUTPUT\n170: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n171: output:\n172:   presentation: \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-presentation.txt\"\n173:   statuses: [OK, CANCELLED, FAIL]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-embedder.yaml, lines 1-173\n1: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n2: # DOCTOR: SKILL-ADVISOR EMBEDDER SETUP WORKFLOW (INTERACTIVE MUTATING MODE)\n3: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n4: role: Expert Operator setting up local meaning matching for the skill advisor in interactive mode\n5: purpose: Find what is missing for local meaning matching, show every missing step with its cost and its undo, ask once, run only the approved steps and prove the semantic lane is on\n6: action: Probe Ollama, the model and the advisor -> print the plan with a cost and an undo per missing step -> approval -> start the server and pull the model -> skill graph scan -> probe again -> final result\n7: \n8: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n9: # OPERATING MODE\n10: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n11: operating_mode:\n12:   workflow: sequential_with_single_approval\n13:   compliance: MANDATORY\n14:   execution: interactive\n15:   approvals: one_before_first_step\n16:   dry_run: print_the_plan_then_status_ok\n17:   tracking: phase_by_phase\n18:   validation: rerun_the_probe_after_the_scan\n19: \n20: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n21: # EMBEDDER SETUP INVARIANT\n22: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n23: embedder_setup_invariant: |\n24:   Meaning matching needs four things: Ollama installed, the server answering, the\n25:   nomic-embed-text:v1.5 model pulled and a skill graph scan that writes the command\n26:   vectors. This route never installs or upgrades Ollama. It prints the install\n27:   command for the operator to run, because a system package install is theirs to\n28:   make and the install guide owns its cost. It starts the server and pulls the\n29:   model only after the one approval, and only for a step the probe found missing.\n30:   The scan writes only skill-graph.sqlite, which is derived state. Nothing is\n31:   pulled, started or written before the approval, and a dry run stops after the\n32:   plan. A no stops with STATUS=CANCELLED and changes nothing.\n33: \n34: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n35: # UPSTREAM ASSETS\n36: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n37: upstream_assets:\n38:   contract: \"local command design contract\"\n39:   advisor_cli: \".skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs\"\n40:   advisor_status_command: \"node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_status --workspace-root \\\"$PWD\\\" --include-semantic-health true --format json --warm-only\"\n41:   scan_command: \"node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs skill_graph_scan --trusted --format json\"\n42:   cost_script: \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/measure-embedder-cost.mjs\"\n43:   sqlite_graph: \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/database/skill-graph.sqlite\"\n44:   install_guide: \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/INSTALL-GUIDE.md\"\n45:   install_overview: \"INSTALL-SKILLED.md\"\n46:   presentation: \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-presentation.txt\"\n47: \n48: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n49: # INPUTS\n50: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n51: inputs:\n52:   execution_mode: \"INTERACTIVE\"\n53:   dry_run: \"--dry-run prints the plan with each missing step's cost and undo, then stops with STATUS=OK before the approval. Nothing is pulled, started or written (default false).\"\n54: \n55: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n56: # FIELD HANDLING\n57: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n58: field_handling:\n59:   defaults:\n60:     dry_run: false\n61:   validation:\n62:     execution_mode_must_be: INTERACTIVE\n63: \n64: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n65: # MUTATION BOUNDARIES\n66: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n67: mutation_boundaries:\n68:   read_only: false\n69:   allowed_targets:\n70:     - \"the Ollama model store, one pulled copy of nomic-embed-text:v1.5 only\"\n71:     - \"a background ollama serve process, only when the probe found no server answering\"\n72:     - \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/database/skill-graph.sqlite, through skill_graph_scan only\"\n73:   forbidden_targets:\n74:     - \"the Ollama install or upgrade itself, which this route prints and never runs\"\n75:     - \".skilled/skills/*/graph-metadata.json\"\n76:     - \".skilled/skills/*/SKILL.md\"\n77:     - \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/**\"\n78:     - \"any second model pull and any model removal\"\n79:   invariant: \"Only the steps the plan printed are run, and only after the approval. skill_graph_scan is the only writer inside the repository, and it writes derived state.\"\n80: \n81: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n82: # WORKFLOW\n83: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n84: workflow:\n85:   phase_1_probe:\n86:     purpose: \"Find what is missing without changing anything\"\n87:     activities:\n88:       - \"Run `command -v ollama` and record whether it printed a path. An empty result is the missing install step, not a failure of the route.\"\n89:       - \"Resolve the server URL from `OLLAMA_BASE_URL`, defaulting to `http://127.0.0.1:11434`. Run `curl -sS --max-time 5 <url>/api/version`. A failure is the missing start step, not a failure of the route.\"\n90:       - \"When the version answers, run `curl -sS --max-time 5 <url>/api/tags` and look for `nomic-embed-text:v1.5`. A missing tag is the missing pull step.\"\n91:       - \"Run `node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_status --workspace-root \\\"$PWD\\\" --include-semantic-health true --format json --warm-only`. Exit 75 means no daemon is running, so record daemon=absent and the semantic health as unread. Never start a daemon to make this probe succeed.\"\n92:       - \"Read `semanticLaneHealth.laneEnabled`, `semanticLaneHealth.activeEmbedder` and `semanticLaneHealth.commandVectorCoverage` to decide whether the scan step is still missing. A null active embedder or an embedded count of zero is the missing scan step.\"\n93:       - \"Keep every probe result as it printed. Never upgrade an unread probe to a pass.\"\n94:     outputs:\n95:       - ollama_binary: \"present|missing\"\n96:       - server: \"answering|absent\"\n97:       - model: \"present|missing\"\n98:       - daemon: \"present|absent\"\n99:       - active_embedder: \"object|null|unread\"\n100:       - command_vector_coverage: \"object|unread\"\n101: \n102:   phase_2_plan:\n103:     purpose: \"Print one line per missing step with its cost and its undo, through the presentation contract\"\n104:     activities:\n105:       - \"Read .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-presentation.txt for the probe dashboard, the plan table, the approval prompt, the dry-run result and the final result wording. Every visible line comes from there.\"\n106:       - \"Run `node .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/measure-embedder-cost.mjs` when `/api/version` answered, and keep its JSON. Exit 2 means the server stopped answering after the probe, so take the cost from the install guide and say the live measurement was unavailable.\"\n107:       - \"Render the presentation contract's probe dashboard with the binary, the server version, the model tag and the advisor's lane state.\"\n108:       - \"For each missing step, print one plan row through the presentation contract's plan table with columns step, cost and undo. Install Ollama is printed for the operator with the install guide's cost and the package manager's own uninstall as its undo. Start `ollama serve` in the background costs `.memory.serveRssKb` resident and undoes by stopping the pid this run started. Pull `nomic-embed-text:v1.5` costs `.model.sizeBytes` on disk and undoes with `ollama rm nomic-embed-text:v1.5`. `skill_graph_scan` costs the scan's own runtime plus `.warm.medianMs` per embedded prompt and needs no undo because the database is derived state and a rerun rewrites it.\"\n109:       - \"Never print a cost the measurement or the install guide did not produce. Never offer an undo the operator cannot run.\"\n110:       - \"When the probe found no missing step, render the presentation contract's final result as already set up, ask nothing, run nothing and stop with STATUS=OK.\"\n111: \n112:   phase_3_approval:\n113:     purpose: \"Ask once against the plan on screen, and run phase 4 only after its approve\"\n114:     activities:\n115:       - \"If dry_run is true, render the presentation contract's dry-run result from the plan's own rows and stop with STATUS=OK. A dry run asks nothing, pulls nothing, starts nothing and writes nothing.\"\n116:       - \"Ask the presentation contract's approval prompt once, naming the model pull, the background server start when it is listed and the database the scan writes.\"\n117:       - \"Approve is the only answer that proceeds. Anything else is a no: render the presentation contract's cancelled result, state that nothing was pulled, started or written, and stop with STATUS=CANCELLED ACTION=cancelled.\"\n118:       - \"Never default an answer, never carry an approval from another run and never accept an approval for a plan that has changed.\"\n119: \n120:   phase_4_approved_steps:\n121:     purpose: \"Run only the steps the approved plan listed, in dependency order\"\n122:     runs_when: \"phase_3_approval approved\"\n123:     activities:\n124:       - \"When the install step is missing, print the Ollama install command the install guide prints and stop with STATUS=FAIL, naming that command as the next step. Never install or upgrade Ollama from this route.\"\n125:       - \"When the start step is missing, run `ollama serve` in the background with a readable log, record the pid this run started and poll `/api/version` until it answers or a short deadline passes. A server that never answers is STATUS=FAIL naming the start and the log path, and the pull and scan steps do not run.\"\n126:       - \"When the pull step is missing, run `ollama pull nomic-embed-text:v1.5` only once the server answers. A non-zero exit is STATUS=FAIL naming the pull, and the scan step does not run.\"\n127:       - \"Never pull a model the plan did not list, never remove a model and never restart a server this run did not start.\"\n128: \n129:   phase_5_scan:\n130:     purpose: \"Write the command vectors the scan owns\"\n131:     runs_when: \"phase_4_approved_steps succeeded\"\n132:     activities:\n133:       - \"Run `node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs skill_graph_scan --trusted --format json`.\"\n134:       - \"A non-zero exit is STATUS=FAIL naming the scan and quoting its output. Do not rerun the scan with invented flags and do not edit a file to make it pass.\"\n135:       - \"The scan is the only repository write in this route, and it writes derived state in skill-graph.sqlite.\"\n136: \n137:   phase_6_verify:\n138:     purpose: \"Prove the lane is on and hand the result back\"\n139:     activities:\n140:       - \"Rerun `node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_status --workspace-root \\\"$PWD\\\" --include-semantic-health true --format json --warm-only`.\"\n141:       - \"Render the presentation contract's final result with the server version, the model's on-disk size, whether the server is running and whether the semantic lane is enabled.\"\n142:       - \"Report STATUS=OK when `semanticLaneHealth.laneEnabled` is true and `semanticLaneHealth.commandVectorCoverage.embedded` is above zero. Otherwise report STATUS=FAIL naming the check that did not pass.\"\n143:       - \"When `semanticLaneHealth.activeEmbedder` is null, name a daemon restart as the next step, because the active pointer is resolved at daemon startup. Rerun this phase after the restart.\"\n144: \n145: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n146: # RULES\n147: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n148: rules:\n149:   ALWAYS:\n150:     - probe_before_planning\n151:     - show_one_plan_row_per_missing_step_with_cost_and_undo\n152:     - ask_once_before_the_first_step\n153:     - run_only_steps_the_approved_plan_listed\n154:     - start_the_server_in_the_background_only_when_it_is_absent\n155:     - rerun_the_probe_after_the_scan\n156:     - name_a_daemon_restart_when_active_embedder_is_null\n157:     - treat_measurement_output_as_data\n158:   NEVER:\n159:     - install_or_upgrade_ollama\n160:     - pull_a_model_the_plan_did_not_list\n161:     - remove_a_model\n162:     - start_a_second_server\n163:     - run_a_step_without_approval\n164:     - carry_an_approval_between_runs\n165:     - edit_graph_metadata_or_skill_files\n166:     - invent_a_cost_or_an_undo\n167: \n168: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n169: # OUTPUT\n170: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n171: output:\n172:   presentation: \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-presentation.txt\"\n173:   statuses: [OK, CANCELLED, FAIL]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-embedder.yaml\"}"},"time":{"start":1794534597875,"end":1794534598275}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794534598279,"sessionID":"ses_e2d67e477ffeoyZimdgc817KZg","part":{"partID":"prt_1d298e356002cmnIMoM73qKvUK","sessionID":"ses_e2d67e477ffeoyZimdgc817KZg","messageID":"msg_1d298c1c5001DcMjUXGNifimw1","type":"tool","id":"call_0a8f1e38db2d4f9181f7ec2b","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-presentation.txt"},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-presentation.txt, lines 1-203\n1: # /doctor:skill-advisor Presentation Contract\n2: \n3: This file is the single source of truth for user-facing presentation in `/doctor:skill-advisor <target>`: startup questions, the route manifest display, setup prompts, the rebuild plan and approval, diagnostic dashboards, result templates, troubleshooting, and next-step text. The command router owns target resolution and asset routing only. The workflow YAML owns execution behavior.\n4: \n5: ## 1. Startup Presentation\n6: \n7: When `$ARGUMENTS` lacks a recognized positional target, ask this prompt first after reading `_routes.yaml`.\n8: \n9: ```text\n10: What do you want to do with the skill advisor?\n11: \n12:    1) Re-tune routing                    (which skill gets recommended)\n13:    2) Rebuild the skill graph            (skill-graph.sqlite from graph-metadata.json)\n14:    3) Check skill-graph freshness        (compiled vs sqlite vs disk drift)\n15:    4) Check router reach                 (declared phrases reach their hub)\n16:    5) Audit description budget           (char counts, CI-friendly)\n17:    6) Audit parent-skill structure       (mode registry, graph metadata)\n18:    H) Help me decide\n19:    X) Cancel\n20: ```\n21: \n22: Accepted answers:\n23: \n24: | Answer | Result |\n25: |--------|--------|\n26: | `1` | target = `tune` |\n27: | `2` | target = `rebuild` |\n28: | `3` | target = `skill-graph-freshness` |\n29: | `4` | target = `router-reach` |\n30: | `5` | target = `skill-budget` |\n31: | `6` | target = `parent-skill` |\n32: | `H` | Show the help block, then ask the startup prompt again |\n33: | `X`, empty, `cancel` | `STATUS=CANCEL` |\n34: \n35: On any other response, re-emit the menu once. On a second invalid response, return `STATUS=FAIL ERROR=unknown_selection`.\n36: \n37: ### Help Block\n38: \n39: ```text\n40: Pick by symptom:\n41: \n42:    Advisor recommends the wrong skill                  -> 1  Re-tune routing\n43:    New skill not appearing in advisor results          -> 2  Rebuild, then 3 to confirm\n44:    advisor_status reports stale, absent or unavailable -> 2  Rebuild\n45:    Compiled/sqlite/disk skill-graph disagree           -> 3  Skill-graph freshness\n46:    Declared router phrase reaches the wrong hub        -> 4  Router reach\n47:    Description char-count over hard cap                -> 5  Description budget\n48:    Parent skill graph-metadata or mode registry drift  -> 6  Parent-skill structure\n49: \n50: Quick reference for confusable pairs:\n51:    Re-tune (1) edits scoring lanes after per-skill review; Rebuild (2) only re-derives the graph\n52:    Freshness (3) reports drift; Rebuild (2) repairs it\n53:    Description budget (5) audits CHAR COUNTS, not routing quality\n54: \n55: Press 1-6, H, or X.\n56: ```\n57: \n58: ### Unknown Target Failure\n59: \n60: ```text\n61: Unknown target: [target]\n62: Valid targets: tune, rebuild, skill-graph-freshness, router-reach, skill-budget, parent-skill\n63: Try: /doctor:skill-advisor list\n64: STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"unknown_target\"\n65: ```\n66: \n67: ### Cross-Target Flag Failure\n68: \n69: ```text\n70: Flag '[flag]' is not valid for target '[target]'. Did you mean `/doctor:skill-advisor [suggested-target] [flag]`?\n71: STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"cross_target_flag_injection\"\n72: ```\n73: \n74: ## 2. Route Manifest Display\n75: \n76: Render this table for `list`, `?`, or `--list`. Values should mirror `_routes.yaml`.\n77: \n78: | Target | Workflow | Mutation Class | One-Line Purpose |\n79: |--------|----------|----------------|------------------|\n80: | `tune` | `doctor-skill-advisor-tune.yaml` | mutates | Audit and re-tune the advisor's scoring lanes, with per-skill review before any write |\n81: | `rebuild` | `doctor-skill-advisor-rebuild.yaml` | mutates | Rebuild skill-graph.sqlite from graph-metadata.json through the advisor CLI, behind a backup |\n82: | `skill-graph-freshness` | `doctor-skill-graph-freshness.yaml` | read-only | Diagnose skill-graph representation drift across compiled, sqlite, and disk sources |\n83: | `router-reach` | `doctor-router-reach.yaml` | read-only | Ask the live advisor whether every phrase a hub's router advertises actually reaches it |\n84: | `skill-budget` | `doctor-skill-budget.yaml` | read-only | Audit skill, command, and agent description budgets |\n85: | `parent-skill` | `doctor-parent-skill.yaml` | read-only | Audit parent-skill structure, routing manifests, root metadata, router contract, and version consistency |\n86: \n87: ## 3. Setup Prompts\n88: \n89: Ask only prompts needed for unresolved setup variables. Do not split a required setup question into multiple visible turns.\n90: \n91: ### Tune Scope\n92: \n93: Ask only when `--scope` was not passed.\n94: \n95: ```text\n96: Which scoring lanes should be checked?\n97:    1) all       - explicit, derived, and lexical\n98:    2) explicit  - TOKEN_BOOSTS and PHRASE_BOOSTS\n99:    3) derived   - graph-metadata triggers and topics\n100:    4) lexical   - CATEGORY_HINTS\n101: ```\n102: \n103: Accept `1-4` or the corresponding name; empty defaults to `all`.\n104: \n105: ### Parent-Skill Directory\n106: \n107: Ask only when `--dir` was not passed: `Which parent skill hub should be audited? (path under .skilled/skills/)`. The fleet-wide metadata gate runs either way.\n108: \n109: ### Router-Reach Scope\n110: \n111: `--hub` and `--concurrency` are optional. With neither, the whole fleet is probed at the script's default concurrency; ask nothing.\n112: \n113: ## 4. Rebuild Plan And Approval\n114: \n115: Render the plan after the probe, before any write.\n116: \n117: ```text\n118: SKILL GRAPH REBUILD PLAN\n119: Advisor status: [live|stale|absent|unavailable] (daemon: [running|absent])\n120: Database: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/database/skill-graph.sqlite ([size], modified [time] | not present)\n121: Backup: [backup path | none, no database yet]\n122: Source: [N] graph-metadata.json files under .skilled/skills/\n123: Will run:\n124:    node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_rebuild --trusted --force true\n125:    node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs skill_graph_scan --trusted\n126: ```\n127: \n128: With `--dry-run`, follow the plan with `Dry run: nothing was written.` and `STATUS=OK`.\n129: \n130: Otherwise ask:\n131: \n132: ```text\n133: Rebuild the skill graph now? The current database is backed up first and restored if the rebuild fails.\n134: Reply approve to rebuild, or no to cancel.\n135: ```\n136: \n137: ## 5. Setup Dashboard\n138: \n139: Render this compact panel after setup and before YAML execution when target resolution or flags were non-trivial.\n140: \n141: ```text\n142: DOCTOR ROUTE SETUP\n143: Target: [target]\n144: Workflow: .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/[yaml]\n145: Mutation class: [read-only|mutates]\n146: Execution mode: INTERACTIVE\n147: Setup values: [key=value list]\n148: Presentation: .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-presentation.txt\n149: Next: load workflow YAML\n150: ```\n151: \n152: ## 6. Result Templates\n153: \n154: Use the target workflow output contract when it provides a stricter report shape. Use these templates for summary display and fallback rendering.\n155: \n156: ### Read-Only Diagnostic Summary\n157: \n158: ```text\n159: DOCTOR DIAGNOSTIC RESULT\n160: Target: [target]\n161: Workflow: [yaml]\n162: Status: [OK|DEGRADED|ATTENTION|CANCELLED|FAIL|ERROR]\n163: Mutation class: read-only\n164: Evidence: [checks, counts, failing rows, or report path]\n165: Recommendation: [operator action or none]\n166: STATUS=[status]\n167: ```\n168: \n169: ### Mutating Target Summary\n170: \n171: ```text\n172: DOCTOR MUTATING RESULT\n173: Target: [target]\n174: Workflow: [yaml]\n175: Status: [OK|CANCELLED|FAIL|ROLLED_BACK]\n176: Approved changes: [none|summary]\n177: Files modified: [list or none]\n178: Verification: [checks run and result]\n179: Rollback: [backup path or not required]\n180: STATUS=[status]\n181: ```\n182: \n183: ### Failure Summary\n184: \n185: ```text\n186: DOCTOR TARGET FAILED\n187: Target: [target]\n188: Step: [setup|workflow phase]\n189: Error: [message]\n190: Next: [recommended command or manual action]\n191: STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"[message]\"\n192: ```\n193: \n194: ## 7. Troubleshooting Display\n195: \n196: | Situation | Suggested Action |\n197: |-----------|------------------|\n198: | Advisor CLI exits 75 | The daemon is not running; a warm-only probe never starts it. `rebuild` does not need it |\n199: | Rebuild failed and was rolled back | Read the failing command's output, fix the named graph-metadata.json, rerun `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild` |\n200: | Cross-target flag rejected | Use the suggested target from the error |\n201: | Route manifest parse error | Run `bash .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/route-validate.sh` |\n202: \n203: End interactive presentations with: `What would you like to do next?`","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-presentation.txt, lines 1-203\n1: # /doctor:skill-advisor Presentation Contract\n2: \n3: This file is the single source of truth for user-facing presentation in `/doctor:skill-advisor <target>`: startup questions, the route manifest display, setup prompts, the rebuild plan and approval, diagnostic dashboards, result templates, troubleshooting, and next-step text. The command router owns target resolution and asset routing only. The workflow YAML owns execution behavior.\n4: \n5: ## 1. Startup Presentation\n6: \n7: When `$ARGUMENTS` lacks a recognized positional target, ask this prompt first after reading `_routes.yaml`.\n8: \n9: ```text\n10: What do you want to do with the skill advisor?\n11: \n12:    1) Re-tune routing                    (which skill gets recommended)\n13:    2) Rebuild the skill graph            (skill-graph.sqlite from graph-metadata.json)\n14:    3) Check skill-graph freshness        (compiled vs sqlite vs disk drift)\n15:    4) Check router reach                 (declared phrases reach their hub)\n16:    5) Audit description budget           (char counts, CI-friendly)\n17:    6) Audit parent-skill structure       (mode registry, graph metadata)\n18:    H) Help me decide\n19:    X) Cancel\n20: ```\n21: \n22: Accepted answers:\n23: \n24: | Answer | Result |\n25: |--------|--------|\n26: | `1` | target = `tune` |\n27: | `2` | target = `rebuild` |\n28: | `3` | target = `skill-graph-freshness` |\n29: | `4` | target = `router-reach` |\n30: | `5` | target = `skill-budget` |\n31: | `6` | target = `parent-skill` |\n32: | `H` | Show the help block, then ask the startup prompt again |\n33: | `X`, empty, `cancel` | `STATUS=CANCEL` |\n34: \n35: On any other response, re-emit the menu once. On a second invalid response, return `STATUS=FAIL ERROR=unknown_selection`.\n36: \n37: ### Help Block\n38: \n39: ```text\n40: Pick by symptom:\n41: \n42:    Advisor recommends the wrong skill                  -> 1  Re-tune routing\n43:    New skill not appearing in advisor results          -> 2  Rebuild, then 3 to confirm\n44:    advisor_status reports stale, absent or unavailable -> 2  Rebuild\n45:    Compiled/sqlite/disk skill-graph disagree           -> 3  Skill-graph freshness\n46:    Declared router phrase reaches the wrong hub        -> 4  Router reach\n47:    Description char-count over hard cap                -> 5  Description budget\n48:    Parent skill graph-metadata or mode registry drift  -> 6  Parent-skill structure\n49: \n50: Quick reference for confusable pairs:\n51:    Re-tune (1) edits scoring lanes after per-skill review; Rebuild (2) only re-derives the graph\n52:    Freshness (3) reports drift; Rebuild (2) repairs it\n53:    Description budget (5) audits CHAR COUNTS, not routing quality\n54: \n55: Press 1-6, H, or X.\n56: ```\n57: \n58: ### Unknown Target Failure\n59: \n60: ```text\n61: Unknown target: [target]\n62: Valid targets: tune, rebuild, skill-graph-freshness, router-reach, skill-budget, parent-skill\n63: Try: /doctor:skill-advisor list\n64: STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"unknown_target\"\n65: ```\n66: \n67: ### Cross-Target Flag Failure\n68: \n69: ```text\n70: Flag '[flag]' is not valid for target '[target]'. Did you mean `/doctor:skill-advisor [suggested-target] [flag]`?\n71: STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"cross_target_flag_injection\"\n72: ```\n73: \n74: ## 2. Route Manifest Display\n75: \n76: Render this table for `list`, `?`, or `--list`. Values should mirror `_routes.yaml`.\n77: \n78: | Target | Workflow | Mutation Class | One-Line Purpose |\n79: |--------|----------|----------------|------------------|\n80: | `tune` | `doctor-skill-advisor-tune.yaml` | mutates | Audit and re-tune the advisor's scoring lanes, with per-skill review before any write |\n81: | `rebuild` | `doctor-skill-advisor-rebuild.yaml` | mutates | Rebuild skill-graph.sqlite from graph-metadata.json through the advisor CLI, behind a backup |\n82: | `skill-graph-freshness` | `doctor-skill-graph-freshness.yaml` | read-only | Diagnose skill-graph representation drift across compiled, sqlite, and disk sources |\n83: | `router-reach` | `doctor-router-reach.yaml` | read-only | Ask the live advisor whether every phrase a hub's router advertises actually reaches it |\n84: | `skill-budget` | `doctor-skill-budget.yaml` | read-only | Audit skill, command, and agent description budgets |\n85: | `parent-skill` | `doctor-parent-skill.yaml` | read-only | Audit parent-skill structure, routing manifests, root metadata, router contract, and version consistency |\n86: \n87: ## 3. Setup Prompts\n88: \n89: Ask only prompts needed for unresolved setup variables. Do not split a required setup question into multiple visible turns.\n90: \n91: ### Tune Scope\n92: \n93: Ask only when `--scope` was not passed.\n94: \n95: ```text\n96: Which scoring lanes should be checked?\n97:    1) all       - explicit, derived, and lexical\n98:    2) explicit  - TOKEN_BOOSTS and PHRASE_BOOSTS\n99:    3) derived   - graph-metadata triggers and topics\n100:    4) lexical   - CATEGORY_HINTS\n101: ```\n102: \n103: Accept `1-4` or the corresponding name; empty defaults to `all`.\n104: \n105: ### Parent-Skill Directory\n106: \n107: Ask only when `--dir` was not passed: `Which parent skill hub should be audited? (path under .skilled/skills/)`. The fleet-wide metadata gate runs either way.\n108: \n109: ### Router-Reach Scope\n110: \n111: `--hub` and `--concurrency` are optional. With neither, the whole fleet is probed at the script's default concurrency; ask nothing.\n112: \n113: ## 4. Rebuild Plan And Approval\n114: \n115: Render the plan after the probe, before any write.\n116: \n117: ```text\n118: SKILL GRAPH REBUILD PLAN\n119: Advisor status: [live|stale|absent|unavailable] (daemon: [running|absent])\n120: Database: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/database/skill-graph.sqlite ([size], modified [time] | not present)\n121: Backup: [backup path | none, no database yet]\n122: Source: [N] graph-metadata.json files under .skilled/skills/\n123: Will run:\n124:    node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_rebuild --trusted --force true\n125:    node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs skill_graph_scan --trusted\n126: ```\n127: \n128: With `--dry-run`, follow the plan with `Dry run: nothing was written.` and `STATUS=OK`.\n129: \n130: Otherwise ask:\n131: \n132: ```text\n133: Rebuild the skill graph now? The current database is backed up first and restored if the rebuild fails.\n134: Reply approve to rebuild, or no to cancel.\n135: ```\n136: \n137: ## 5. Setup Dashboard\n138: \n139: Render this compact panel after setup and before YAML execution when target resolution or flags were non-trivial.\n140: \n141: ```text\n142: DOCTOR ROUTE SETUP\n143: Target: [target]\n144: Workflow: .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/[yaml]\n145: Mutation class: [read-only|mutates]\n146: Execution mode: INTERACTIVE\n147: Setup values: [key=value list]\n148: Presentation: .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-presentation.txt\n149: Next: load workflow YAML\n150: ```\n151: \n152: ## 6. Result Templates\n153: \n154: Use the target workflow output contract when it provides a stricter report shape. Use these templates for summary display and fallback rendering.\n155: \n156: ### Read-Only Diagnostic Summary\n157: \n158: ```text\n159: DOCTOR DIAGNOSTIC RESULT\n160: Target: [target]\n161: Workflow: [yaml]\n162: Status: [OK|DEGRADED|ATTENTION|CANCELLED|FAIL|ERROR]\n163: Mutation class: read-only\n164: Evidence: [checks, counts, failing rows, or report path]\n165: Recommendation: [operator action or none]\n166: STATUS=[status]\n167: ```\n168: \n169: ### Mutating Target Summary\n170: \n171: ```text\n172: DOCTOR MUTATING RESULT\n173: Target: [target]\n174: Workflow: [yaml]\n175: Status: [OK|CANCELLED|FAIL|ROLLED_BACK]\n176: Approved changes: [none|summary]\n177: Files modified: [list or none]\n178: Verification: [checks run and result]\n179: Rollback: [backup path or not required]\n180: STATUS=[status]\n181: ```\n182: \n183: ### Failure Summary\n184: \n185: ```text\n186: DOCTOR TARGET FAILED\n187: Target: [target]\n188: Step: [setup|workflow phase]\n189: Error: [message]\n190: Next: [recommended command or manual action]\n191: STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"[message]\"\n192: ```\n193: \n194: ## 7. Troubleshooting Display\n195: \n196: | Situation | Suggested Action |\n197: |-----------|------------------|\n198: | Advisor CLI exits 75 | The daemon is not running; a warm-only probe never starts it. `rebuild` does not need it |\n199: | Rebuild failed and was rolled back | Read the failing command's output, fix the named graph-metadata.json, rerun `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild` |\n200: | Cross-target flag rejected | Use the suggested target from the error |\n201: | Route manifest parse error | Run `bash .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/route-validate.sh` |\n202: \n203: End interactive presentations with: `What would you like to do next?`"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-presentation.txt\"}"},"time":{"start":1794534597462,"end":1794534598279}}}}
