s_e2d67e477ffeoyZimdgc817KZg\",\"part\":{\"partID\":\"prt_1d298e356002cmnIMoM73qKvUK\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_e2d67e477ffeoyZimdgc817KZg\",\"messageID\":\"msg_1d298c1c5001DcMjUXGNifimw1\",\"type\":\"tool\",\"id\":\"call_0a8f1e38db2d4f9181f7ec2b\",\"tool\":\"read\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-presentation.txt\"},\"output\":\"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-presentation.txt, lines 1-203\\n1: # /doctor:skill-advisor Presentation Contract\\n2: \\n3: This file is the single source of truth for user-facing presentation in `/doctor:skill-advisor <target>`: startup questions, the route manifest display, setup prompts, the rebuild plan and approval, diagnostic dashboards, result templates, troubleshooting, and next-step text. The command router owns target resolution and asset routing only. The workflow YAML owns execution behavior.\\n4: \\n5: ## 1. Startup Presentation\\n6: \\n7: When `$ARGUMENTS` lacks a recognized positional target, ask this prompt first after reading `_routes.yaml`.\\n8: \\n9: ```text\\n10: What do you want to do with the skill advisor?\\n11: \\n12:    1) Re-tune routing                    (which skill gets recommended)\\n13:    2) Rebuild the skill graph            (skill-graph.sqlite from graph-metadata.json)\\n14:    3) Check skill-graph freshness        (compiled vs sqlite vs disk drift)\\n15:    4) Check router reach                 (declared phrases reach their hub)\\n16:    5) Audit description budget           (char counts, CI-friendly)\\n17:    6) Audit parent-skill structure       (mode registry, graph metadata)\\n18:    H) Help me decide\\n19:    X) Cancel\\n20: ```\\n21: \\n22: Accepted answers:\\n23: \\n24: | Answer | Result |\\n25: |--------|--------|\\n26: | `1` | target = `tune` |\\n27: