{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794534626191,"sessionID":"ses_e2d67e477ffeoyZimdgc817KZg","part":{"id":"prt_1d299538f0012ZxL1y6T4b2RkE","sessionID":"ses_e2d67e477ffeoyZimdgc817KZg","messageID":"msg_1d2993f8b001G3HB3IBsG8X6BQ","type":"step-start","snapshot":"9d3d296e5c0642fa37e994d0d818f82ebd71e0f9"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794534628770,"sessionID":"ses_e2d67e477ffeoyZimdgc817KZg","part":{"partID":"prt_1d2995bef001ut50KJZEDtSWdP","sessionID":"ses_e2d67e477ffeoyZimdgc817KZg","messageID":"msg_1d2993f8b001G3HB3IBsG8X6BQ","type":"tool","id":"call_3406c0ca21d5466398583688","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt","limit":120},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt, lines 1-107\n1: # /doctor:setup Presentation Contract\n2: \n3: This file is the single source of truth for user-facing presentation in `/doctor:setup`: the argument failure, the doctor target list, the per-leg result table, result templates, and next-step text. The command router owns asset routing only. The workflow YAML owns execution behavior.\n4: \n5: ## 1. Argument Failure\n6: \n7: ```text\n8: Unknown argument: [argument]\n9: /doctor:setup takes no target and no flag. Run /doctor:setup on its own.\n10: STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"unknown_argument\"\n11: ```\n12: \n13: ## 2. Doctor Target List\n14: \n15: Render this table first, before any leg runs.\n16: \n17: | Command | What it checks |\n18: |---------|----------------|\n19: | `/doctor:setup` | This overview: the doctor target list and the five read-only setup legs |\n20: | `/doctor:helper [<problem in plain words>] [--json]` | Rank the doctor commands that fit a described problem, with the class and the reason on every line |\n21: | `/doctor:env list` | The documented environment switches and where each value comes from |\n22: | `/doctor:update` | Whether a newer spec-kit release is available (bare runs the read-only check) |\n23: | `/doctor:git setup` | Whether the sk-git install, hooks, trust and standards are live |\n24: | `/doctor:git hooks` | Which shipped git hook gates are on or off, and switching one |\n25: | `/doctor:git standards` | The commit, PR and branch rules in .sk-git/ |\n26: | `/doctor:sk-code setup` | The sk-code setup battery, with a repair command per failing leg |\n27: | `/doctor:sk-code quality` | The repository quality config the gate reads with its tools, errors and disabled hygiene rules, then creating `.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-quality/repository/quality.json` once |\n28: | `/doctor:ci report` | Lists every workflow with its switch state, trigger, filters and drift flags, read against the repository CI profile; `scaffold` and `toggle` are the confirmed action routes |\n29: | `/doctor:sk-skill check [<name-or-path>] [--json] [--into-hub <hub>]` | How far one skill, or the whole fleet, is from the Skilled format, row by row, with the repair for each finding |\n30: | `/doctor:sk-skill convert <name-or-path> [--dry-run]` | Moving one skill to the Skilled format: the plan, one yes per write, the backup, the write and the engine's undo block |\n31: | `/doctor:agents-md [check|embed|restore] [--json] [--root <dir>] [--dry-run]` | The root instruction file: which shipped sections are current, embedding the template over a printed plan and its digest, and putting one recorded run back |\n32: | `/doctor:speckit` | The generated trigger index, its lookup and the ripgrep recipes |\n33: | `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` | Whether each runtime's agent, command, prompt and hook mirrors match .skilled |\n34: | `/doctor:skill-advisor tune` | Advisor recommendation quality and scoring tuning |\n35: | `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild` | Rebuilding the skill graph database |\n36: | `/doctor:skill-advisor skill-budget` | Skill description character budgets |\n37: | `/doctor:skill-advisor parent-skill` | A parent skill hub's structure and registry |\n38: | `/doctor:skill-advisor skill-graph-freshness` | Drift between the compiled, SQLite and on-disk skill graph |\n39: | `/doctor:skill-advisor router-reach` | Whether each declared routing phrase reaches its hub |\n40: | `/doctor:deep-loop` | Deep-loop coverage graphs and convergence for research, review and council runs |\n41: | `/doctor:mcp` | Code Mode install and debug, its UTCP configuration and runtime registration |\n42: | `/doctor:install [--root <dir>] [--runtimes <list>] [--json]` | Putting Skilled into your own project repo: the build check, what is already linked, and the ordered setup commands to run |\n43: | `/doctor:symlink [check|link|unlink] [--json] [--root <dir>]` | The framework links in a project repo: which runtime folders are linked, broken or missing, linking them over a printed plan and its digest, and undoing one recorded run |\n44: | `/doctor:overlay [status|apply|repin] [--json] [--root <dir>]` | A vendored Skilled tree's own overlays: which destinations are out of sync and why, then putting them back, capturing one live edit, or re-pinning the tree to a newer upstream commit over a staged plan, after one yes |\n45: \n46: ## 3. Per-Leg Result Table\n47: \n48: Render one row per leg, in the workflow's order.\n49: \n50: | Leg | Command | Result | Repair |\n51: |-----|---------|--------|--------|\n52: | [leg] | [check-only command] | [PASS|FAIL|SKIP|DEGRADED|ERROR] | [the doctor command that repairs it or shows why, or none] |\n53: \n54: | Leg | Repair when it fails |\n55: |-----|----------------------|\n56: | sk-code | `/doctor:sk-code setup` |\n57: | sk-git | `/doctor:git setup` |\n58: | trigger-index | `/doctor:speckit` |\n59: | runtime-mirrors | `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` |\n60: | advisor | Stale build: `npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime run build`. Other FAIL or DEGRADED results: `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild`. |\n61: \n62: ## 4. Result Templates\n63: \n64: ### Summary\n65: \n66: ```text\n67: DOCTOR DIAGNOSTIC RESULT\n68: Target: setup\n69: Status: [OK|FAIL|ERROR]\n70: Mutation class: read-only\n71: Evidence: [N] legs, [N] passed, [N] failed, [N] skipped, [N] degraded, [N] errors\n72: Recommendation: [the doctor command for each failing or degraded leg, or none]\n73: Last session hop: [the first line `session-relaunch.cjs history --last 1` printed, or no hop recorded yet]\n74: [open notes: N handoff notes not claimed yet, oldest <filename>; shown only when history printed it]\n75: [the line `session-relaunch.cjs window` printed: Claude context window: N tokens, or Claude context window: none configured with the two settings that supply one]\n76: [orphans: N, about M MB; list them with node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/orphan-process-check.cjs --reap]\n77: STATUS=[status]\n78: ```\n79: \n80: The last session hop line is informational. It shows when a session last handed over, kept, claimed or finished a handoff, and it never changes the status. The open notes line appears only while a handoff note is still open, so a hand-over nobody finished stays visible.\n81: The Claude context window line is informational and never changes the status. It shows the window the Claude relaunch nudge measures against. When no window is configured it names `autoCompactWindow` and `SESSION_RELAUNCH_WINDOW_TOKENS`, and the nudge stays off until one is set or a `[1m]` model runs.\n82: The orphan line is informational only and never changes the doctor status. A model server kept on purpose with `SPECKIT_HF_MODEL_SERVER_ORPHAN_REAP=0` also shows as unsupervised, so do not reap it. With no orphan processes, print `orphans: none`. Run the listed `--reap` command to see each process, then use its confirmation command with `--yes` only when those are the processes to stop.\n83: \n84: ### Failure Summary\n85: \n86: ```text\n87: DOCTOR TARGET FAILED\n88: Target: setup\n89: Step: [leg]\n90: Error: [message]\n91: Next: [recommended command or manual action]\n92: STATUS=ERROR ERROR=\"[message]\"\n93: ```\n94: \n95: ## 5. Troubleshooting Display\n96: \n97: | Situation | Suggested Action |\n98: |-----------|------------------|\n99: | A leg reports FAIL | Run the doctor command in that leg's Repair cell, then rerun `/doctor:setup` |\n100: | The advisor leg reports SKIP | Exit 75 has no `staleDistWarning` in stderr JSON. The advisor daemon is stopped because `--warm-only` does not start it |\n101: | The advisor leg reports FAIL for a stale build | Exit 75 includes `staleDistWarning` in stderr JSON. Run `npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime run build` |\n102: | The advisor leg reports DEGRADED | Exit 0 has `data.freshness` other than `live`. The skill graph is not live. Run `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild` |\n103: | The sk-git leg reports DEGRADED | No sk-git check failed, but one is unknown or a gate is saved off. Run `/doctor:git setup` to see which. On a runtime the battery cannot name, the AI-tool check stays unknown |\n104: | The trigger-index leg reports stale documents | Run `/doctor:speckit` to see which documents are stale |\n105: | Route manifest parse error | Run `bash .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/route-validate.sh` |\n106: \n107: End interactive presentations with: `What would you like to do next?`","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt, lines 1-107\n1: # /doctor:setup Presentation Contract\n2: \n3: This file is the single source of truth for user-facing presentation in `/doctor:setup`: the argument failure, the doctor target list, the per-leg result table, result templates, and next-step text. The command router owns asset routing only. The workflow YAML owns execution behavior.\n4: \n5: ## 1. Argument Failure\n6: \n7: ```text\n8: Unknown argument: [argument]\n9: /doctor:setup takes no target and no flag. Run /doctor:setup on its own.\n10: STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"unknown_argument\"\n11: ```\n12: \n13: ## 2. Doctor Target List\n14: \n15: Render this table first, before any leg runs.\n16: \n17: | Command | What it checks |\n18: |---------|----------------|\n19: | `/doctor:setup` | This overview: the doctor target list and the five read-only setup legs |\n20: | `/doctor:helper [<problem in plain words>] [--json]` | Rank the doctor commands that fit a described problem, with the class and the reason on every line |\n21: | `/doctor:env list` | The documented environment switches and where each value comes from |\n22: | `/doctor:update` | Whether a newer spec-kit release is available (bare runs the read-only check) |\n23: | `/doctor:git setup` | Whether the sk-git install, hooks, trust and standards are live |\n24: | `/doctor:git hooks` | Which shipped git hook gates are on or off, and switching one |\n25: | `/doctor:git standards` | The commit, PR and branch rules in .sk-git/ |\n26: | `/doctor:sk-code setup` | The sk-code setup battery, with a repair command per failing leg |\n27: | `/doctor:sk-code quality` | The repository quality config the gate reads with its tools, errors and disabled hygiene rules, then creating `.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-quality/repository/quality.json` once |\n28: | `/doctor:ci report` | Lists every workflow with its switch state, trigger, filters and drift flags, read against the repository CI profile; `scaffold` and `toggle` are the confirmed action routes |\n29: | `/doctor:sk-skill check [<name-or-path>] [--json] [--into-hub <hub>]` | How far one skill, or the whole fleet, is from the Skilled format, row by row, with the repair for each finding |\n30: | `/doctor:sk-skill convert <name-or-path> [--dry-run]` | Moving one skill to the Skilled format: the plan, one yes per write, the backup, the write and the engine's undo block |\n31: | `/doctor:agents-md [check|embed|restore] [--json] [--root <dir>] [--dry-run]` | The root instruction file: which shipped sections are current, embedding the template over a printed plan and its digest, and putting one recorded run back |\n32: | `/doctor:speckit` | The generated trigger index, its lookup and the ripgrep recipes |\n33: | `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` | Whether each runtime's agent, command, prompt and hook mirrors match .skilled |\n34: | `/doctor:skill-advisor tune` | Advisor recommendation quality and scoring tuning |\n35: | `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild` | Rebuilding the skill graph database |\n36: | `/doctor:skill-advisor skill-budget` | Skill description character budgets |\n37: | `/doctor:skill-advisor parent-skill` | A parent skill hub's structure and registry |\n38: | `/doctor:skill-advisor skill-graph-freshness` | Drift between the compiled, SQLite and on-disk skill graph |\n39: | `/doctor:skill-advisor router-reach` | Whether each declared routing phrase reaches its hub |\n40: | `/doctor:deep-loop` | Deep-loop coverage graphs and convergence for research, review and council runs |\n41: | `/doctor:mcp` | Code Mode install and debug, its UTCP configuration and runtime registration |\n42: | `/doctor:install [--root <dir>] [--runtimes <list>] [--json]` | Putting Skilled into your own project repo: the build check, what is already linked, and the ordered setup commands to run |\n43: | `/doctor:symlink [check|link|unlink] [--json] [--root <dir>]` | The framework links in a project repo: which runtime folders are linked, broken or missing, linking them over a printed plan and its digest, and undoing one recorded run |\n44: | `/doctor:overlay [status|apply|repin] [--json] [--root <dir>]` | A vendored Skilled tree's own overlays: which destinations are out of sync and why, then putting them back, capturing one live edit, or re-pinning the tree to a newer upstream commit over a staged plan, after one yes |\n45: \n46: ## 3. Per-Leg Result Table\n47: \n48: Render one row per leg, in the workflow's order.\n49: \n50: | Leg | Command | Result | Repair |\n51: |-----|---------|--------|--------|\n52: | [leg] | [check-only command] | [PASS|FAIL|SKIP|DEGRADED|ERROR] | [the doctor command that repairs it or shows why, or none] |\n53: \n54: | Leg | Repair when it fails |\n55: |-----|----------------------|\n56: | sk-code | `/doctor:sk-code setup` |\n57: | sk-git | `/doctor:git setup` |\n58: | trigger-index | `/doctor:speckit` |\n59: | runtime-mirrors | `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` |\n60: | advisor | Stale build: `npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime run build`. Other FAIL or DEGRADED results: `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild`. |\n61: \n62: ## 4. Result Templates\n63: \n64: ### Summary\n65: \n66: ```text\n67: DOCTOR DIAGNOSTIC RESULT\n68: Target: setup\n69: Status: [OK|FAIL|ERROR]\n70: Mutation class: read-only\n71: Evidence: [N] legs, [N] passed, [N] failed, [N] skipped, [N] degraded, [N] errors\n72: Recommendation: [the doctor command for each failing or degraded leg, or none]\n73: Last session hop: [the first line `session-relaunch.cjs history --last 1` printed, or no hop recorded yet]\n74: [open notes: N handoff notes not claimed yet, oldest <filename>; shown only when history printed it]\n75: [the line `session-relaunch.cjs window` printed: Claude context window: N tokens, or Claude context window: none configured with the two settings that supply one]\n76: [orphans: N, about M MB; list them with node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/orphan-process-check.cjs --reap]\n77: STATUS=[status]\n78: ```\n79: \n80: The last session hop line is informational. It shows when a session last handed over, kept, claimed or finished a handoff, and it never changes the status. The open notes line appears only while a handoff note is still open, so a hand-over nobody finished stays visible.\n81: The Claude context window line is informational and never changes the status. It shows the window the Claude relaunch nudge measures against. When no window is configured it names `autoCompactWindow` and `SESSION_RELAUNCH_WINDOW_TOKENS`, and the nudge stays off until one is set or a `[1m]` model runs.\n82: The orphan line is informational only and never changes the doctor status. A model server kept on purpose with `SPECKIT_HF_MODEL_SERVER_ORPHAN_REAP=0` also shows as unsupervised, so do not reap it. With no orphan processes, print `orphans: none`. Run the listed `--reap` command to see each process, then use its confirmation command with `--yes` only when those are the processes to stop.\n83: \n84: ### Failure Summary\n85: \n86: ```text\n87: DOCTOR TARGET FAILED\n88: Target: setup\n89: Step: [leg]\n90: Error: [message]\n91: Next: [recommended command or manual action]\n92: STATUS=ERROR ERROR=\"[message]\"\n93: ```\n94: \n95: ## 5. Troubleshooting Display\n96: \n97: | Situation | Suggested Action |\n98: |-----------|------------------|\n99: | A leg reports FAIL | Run the doctor command in that leg's Repair cell, then rerun `/doctor:setup` |\n100: | The advisor leg reports SKIP | Exit 75 has no `staleDistWarning` in stderr JSON. The advisor daemon is stopped because `--warm-only` does not start it |\n101: | The advisor leg reports FAIL for a stale build | Exit 75 includes `staleDistWarning` in stderr JSON. Run `npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime run build` |\n102: | The advisor leg reports DEGRADED | Exit 0 has `data.freshness` other than `live`. The skill graph is not live. Run `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild` |\n103: | The sk-git leg reports DEGRADED | No sk-git check failed, but one is unknown or a gate is saved off. Run `/doctor:git setup` to see which. On a runtime the battery cannot name, the AI-tool check stays unknown |\n104: | The trigger-index leg reports stale documents | Run `/doctor:speckit` to see which documents are stale |\n105: | Route manifest parse error | Run `bash .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/route-validate.sh` |\n106: \n107: End interactive presentations with: `What would you like to do next?`"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt\",\"limit\":120}"},"time":{"start":1794534628335,"end":1794534628770}}}}
