-advisor embedder` otherwise, and the route writes nothing | `rg -n \"Leg embedder\" DOC/assets/doctor-setup.yaml`, the T042 leg output and `bash DOC/scripts/tests/run-all.sh` reports 0 failed | Unmet | - |\n59: | AC-004 | REQ-004 | Given `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder`, When it runs with `--dry-run` or the user declines, Then it prints a plan with a cost and an undo per step and runs no step, and on approve it runs only the approved steps, never installs Ollama and ends with a scan and a status | `node DOC/scripts/tests/skill-advisor-route-contract.test.cjs` exits 0, `bash DOC/scripts/route-validate.sh` exits 0 and the T043 dry-run transcript | Unmet | - |\n60: | AC-005 | REQ-005 | Given an injected adapter, When it answers warm, answers cold inside the deadline, is absent, lacks the model or never answers, Then the first two score with a cosine, the others return the no-embedder result inside the deadline plus 100 ms with reasons `prompt_embedding_unreachable`, `prompt_embedding_model_missing` and `prompt_embedding_timeout` | `npx vitest run tests/semantic-prompt-embedding-degrade.vitest.ts` in `ADV` reports 7 passed | Unmet | - |\n61: | AC-006 | REQ-006 | Given `/doctor:install` and the install guides, When a user runs or reads them, Then the checklist prints the embedder route as step 5 before `/doctor:setup` as step 6, and both guides say the install sets up meaning matching by default behind a yes, give the measured cost with its date and say a no keeps a phrase-only install | `node DOC/scripts/tests/doctor-install-contract.test.cjs` exits 0, `rg -n \"meaning matching\\|skill-advisor embedder\\|semantic_lane_off\" INSTALL-SKILLED.md`, `rg -n \"skill-advisor embedder\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/INSTALL-GUIDE.md` and each cost number found in `scratch/cost-warm.json` or `scratch/cost-cold.json` | Unmet | - |\n62: | AC-007 | REQ-007 | Given a call scored without a prompt vector, When the recommendation is returned, Then `warnings` holds `semantic_lane_off:<reason>` and the brief is unchanged | The warning row in `tests/semantic-prompt-embedding-degrade.vitest.ts` and the golden brief tests in `npm test` in `ADV` | Unmet | - |\n63: | AC-008 | REQ-008 | Given the change, When the default capture, the floor, the rollup and both suites run, Then they print typed 24 of 44, tune combined 9 of 45, holdout 0 of 44, false offers 0 of 35, `[159,50,20,5]` and `{\"ask\":17,\"run\":7,\"start\":20}`, with 0 failed | `node $C \\| $M`, `capture-scorer-eval-baseline.mjs` through the phase 003 jq projection, `R`, `npm test` in `ADV` and `bash DOC/scripts/tests/run-all.sh` | Unmet | - |\n64: | AC-009 | REQ-009 | Given the route's bridge active and a rescan, When the real-embedding capture and the phrase-reach probe run, Then tune combined is 14 of 45, holdout 2 of 44, typed 24 of 44, false offers 0 of 35, `vec_cmd_768` matches the entries with `embeddingText` and the probe exits 0 | `node $C --real-embedding \\| $M`, the T031 count comparison and `node DOC/scripts/doctor-phrase-reach.cjs` | Unmet | - |\n65: | AC-010 | REQ-010 | Given three before and three after hook runs over the 44 tune prompts, When the middle runs are compared, Then the median grew by at most 25 ms and the p95 by at most 40 ms | The six `scratch/hook-latency-*.json` files | Unmet | - |\n66: | AC-011 | REQ-011 | Given the advisor install guide, When a user looks for embedder health, Then it says `includeEmbeddingsHealth` probes hf-local only and names `includeSemanticHealth` | `rg -n \"includeEmbeddingsHealth\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/INSTALL-GUIDE.md` prints a line naming hf-local | Unmet | - |\n67: \n68: ### Status values\n69: \n70: | Value | Meaning |\n71: |-------|---------|\n72: | `Met` | Verified. The Verification cell names evidence that was actually observed. |\n73: | `Unmet` | Not yet satisfied. Blocks closure. |\n74: | `Waived` | Deliberately not pursued. Requires an ADR in the Waiver cell. |\n75: | `Superseded` | Replaced by a different criterion or decision. Requires an ADR in the Waiver cell. |\n76: \n77: ### Waiver cell\n78: \n79: Write `-` when the row is `Met` or `Unmet`. Write `ADR-NNN` when the row is\n80: `Waived` or `Superseded`, naming a decision record that exists in\n81: `decision-record.md`. A waiver naming an ADR that is not there fails validation:\n82: the point of a waiver is that someone recorded the reasoning, so an unbacked\n83: waiver is treated as an unmet criterion rather than as a pass.\n84: <!-- /ANCHOR:criteria -->\n85: \n86: ---\n87: \n88: <!-- ANCHOR:closure -->\n89: ## 3. CLOSURE STATEMENT\n90: \n91: **Closeable:** No\n92: \n93: The phase is planned and no build has started. The operator answered every planning question on 2026-11-12.\n94: <!-- /ANCHOR:closure -->"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/008-embedder-setup-and-cost/acceptance-criteria.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794534656646,"end":1794534656751}}}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1794534659412,"sessionID":"ses_e2d67e477ffeoyZimdgc817KZg","part":{"id":"prt_1d299d554001CJZTMA3M9AExy2","sessionID":"ses_e2d67e477ffeoyZimdgc817KZg","messageID":"msg_1d299c18d001TzgdCLfGrLQDLI","type":"step-finish","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"c9bbe12028bffd7c704b7c789c1b550ed74c575d","cost":0,"tokens":{"input":731,"output":94,"reasoning":26,"cache":{"read":68224,"write":0}}}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794534661469,"sessionID":"ses_e2d67e477ffeoyZimdgc817KZg","part":{"id":"prt_1d299dd5d001wffeCrRKd0WiOm","sessionID":"ses_e2d67e477ffeoyZimdgc817KZg","messageID":"msg_1d299d55b001tblPt680ZBphtD","type":"step-start","snapshot":"83cb6538887994f8cba793e18579da328eb5a4ce"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794534665164,"sessionID":"ses_e2d67e477ffeoyZimdgc817KZg","part":{"partID":"prt_1d299e85a002oc4CYpHynmksrB","sessionID":"ses_e2d67e477ffeoyZimdgc817KZg","messageID":"msg_1d299d55b001tblPt680ZBphtD","type":"tool","id":"call_3332570212c24739954e1ef9","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-update-presentation.txt","limit":90},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-update-presentation.txt, lines 1-90\n1: # /doctor:update Presentation Contract\n2: \n3: This file is the single source of truth for user-facing wording and layout in `/doctor:update check`, `align`, `apply`, `compat`, `rollback` and `record-base`. The router owns argument parsing and action routing. Each workflow YAML owns execution behavior.\n4: \n5: ## 1. Action and Flag Errors\n6: \n7: ### Unknown action\n8: \n9: ```text\n10: ERROR: /doctor:update does not recognize action \"[action]\".\n11: Choose check, align, apply, compat, rollback or record-base.\n12: No workflow was started.\n13: ```\n14: \n15: ### Cross-action or unknown flag\n16: \n17: ```text\n18: ERROR: [flag] is not valid for /doctor:update [action].\n19: Accepted flags: [flags for this action]\n20: No workflow was loaded and no engine command was run.\n21: ```\n22: \n23: Accepted flags by action:\n24: \n25: | Action | Flags |\n26: |--------|-------|\n27: | check | `--json`, `--release=<tag>`, `--scope=all|<unit-key,...>`, `--offline`, `--include-prerelease`, `--remote=<name-or-url>` |\n28: | align | `--release=<tag>`, `--scope=all|<unit-key,...>`, `--offline`, `--dry-run`, `--include-prerelease`, `--remote=<name-or-url>` |\n29: | apply | `--decisions=<path>`, `--dry-run`, `--release=<tag>`, `--scope=all|<unit-key,...>`, `--include-prerelease`, `--offline`, `--remote=<name-or-url>` |\n30: | compat | `--dry-run`, `--offline` |\n31: | rollback | `--run=<runDir>`, `--dry-run` |\n32: | record-base | `--release=<tag>`, `--remote=<name-or-url>`, `--scope=all|<unit-key,...>`, `--offline`, `--include-prerelease`, `--trust-release`, `--dry-run` |\n33: \n34: Latest-upstream resolution takes stable `vN.N.N.N` tags only. `--include-prerelease` also admits `vN.N.N.N-<pre>` tags. Both compare version segments as numbers. A tag named with `--release` is used as given.\n35: \n36: A check may fetch release commits it lacks into the git object store. That changes no checkout file or ref. Pass --offline to prevent every fetch.\n37: \n38: Bare `/doctor:update` runs `check`. There are no `:auto` or `:confirm` suffixes.\n39: \n40: ## 2. Check Dashboard\n41: \n42: Render the engine report using this layout. Use `UNKNOWN` when upstream latest or the overall report status is unknown. Never treat unavailable upstream data as proof that the checkout is current.\n43: \n44: When the operator passes `--json`, return the engine report as one JSON document and omit the prose dashboard and next steps.\n45: \n46: ```text\n47: Spec-kit Release Check\n48: \n49: Release position: [ahead|behind|at-release|unknown] [release tag or UNKNOWN]\n50: Upstream latest: [tag or UNKNOWN]\n51: Checkout: [head]  Ahead: [count]  Behind: [count]  Dirty: [yes|no]\n52: Report status: [status]\n53: \n54: Quiet units: [current count] current, [local count] local (no action)\n55: \n56: | Status | Unit | Kind | File changes | Changelog highlights |\n57: |--------|------|------|--------------|----------------------|\n58: | [update|new|customized|conflict|removed|blocked|downgrade|unknown] | [unit] | [kind] | [class counts] | [highlights or none found] |\n59: \n60: Next steps\n61: [action-specific next step]\n62: ```\n63: \n64: Files the engine classes `generated` (a leaf manifest, the trigger index and its sidecars, a compiled-route activation manifest, or a graph-metadata change inside its `derived` block) were rewritten by a generator. They never count as customizations. Include them in class counts and offer no decision.\n65: \n66: Show a row for each unit that is not `current` or `local`, grouped by status. Combine `current` and `local` into the quiet line and include both counts. Include counts for statuses with no matching unit as zero in the summary when the engine report provides status counts. Preserve an unexpected unit status visibly as `unknown`. Show available changelog highlights from the selected release and unit. If upstream latest is unavailable, display `UNKNOWN` and its engine error when present.\n67: \n68: ### Check next steps\n69: \n70: Use the applicable line or lines:\n71: \n72: ```text\n73: Customized or conflict units need decisions: /doctor:update align [same release and scope flags]\n74: Removed units need a decision review: /doctor:update align [same release and scope flags]\n75: Only update or new units need writes: /doctor:update apply [same release and scope flags]\n76: Removed, blocked or unknown units need review before applying: inspect the status details, then choose align or apply as appropriate.\n77: Downgrade units are older in the selected release than in this checkout. Apply never writes them. Roll back the apply that took the newer release, or use git, to return to an older release.\n78: Advisor graph rebuild after an update: /doctor:skill-advisor rebuild\n79: Shipped AGENTS.md sections after an update: /doctor:agents-md check\n80: No selected units need an update.\n81: ```\n82: \n83: When offering apply without a decisions file, add this note if no earlier alignment run is known:\n84: \n85: ```text\n86: No alignment run is needed for update and new units. /doctor:update apply plans from the current check, writes only those units, and re-checks each file against its base before writing. Customized or conflicting units are skipped until /doctor:update align records decisions for them.\n87: ```\n88: \n89: When the report's `baseRecording.needed` is true, add:\n90: \n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 91]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-update-presentation.txt, lines 1-90\n1: # /doctor:update Presentation Contract\n2: \n3: This file is the single source of truth for user-facing wording and layout in `/doctor:update check`, `align`, `apply`, `compat`, `rollback` and `record-base`. The router owns argument parsing and action routing. Each workflow YAML owns execution behavior.\n4: \n5: ## 1. Action and Flag Errors\n6: \n7: ### Unknown action\n8: \n9: ```text\n10: ERROR: /doctor:update does not recognize action \"[action]\".\n11: Choose check, align, apply, compat, rollback or record-base.\n12: No workflow was started.\n13: ```\n14: \n15: ### Cross-action or unknown flag\n16: \n17: ```text\n18: ERROR: [flag] is not valid for /doctor:update [action].\n19: Accepted flags: [flags for this action]\n20: No workflow was loaded and no engine command was run.\n21: ```\n22: \n23: Accepted flags by action:\n24: \n25: | Action | Flags |\n26: |--------|-------|\n27: | check | `--json`, `--release=<tag>`, `--scope=all|<unit-key,...>`, `--offline`, `--include-prerelease`, `--remote=<name-or-url>` |\n28: | align | `--release=<tag>`, `--scope=all|<unit-key,...>`, `--offline`, `--dry-run`, `--include-prerelease`, `--remote=<name-or-url>` |\n29: | apply | `--decisions=<path>`, `--dry-run`, `--release=<tag>`, `--scope=all|<unit-key,...>`, `--include-prerelease`, `--offline`, `--remote=<name-or-url>` |\n30: | compat | `--dry-run`, `--offline` |\n31: | rollback | `--run=<runDir>`, `--dry-run` |\n32: | record-base | `--release=<tag>`, `--remote=<name-or-url>`, `--scope=all|<unit-key,...>`, `--offline`, `--include-prerelease`, `--trust-release`, `--dry-run` |\n33: \n34: Latest-upstream resolution takes stable `vN.N.N.N` tags only. `--include-prerelease` also admits `vN.N.N.N-<pre>` tags. Both compare version segments as numbers. A tag named with `--release` is used as given.\n35: \n36: A check may fetch release commits it lacks into the git object store. That changes no checkout file or ref. Pass --offline to prevent every fetch.\n37: \n38: Bare `/doctor:update` runs `check`. There are no `:auto` or `:confirm` suffixes.\n39: \n40: ## 2. Check Dashboard\n41: \n42: Render the engine report using this layout. Use `UNKNOWN` when upstream latest or the overall report status is unknown. Never treat unavailable upstream data as proof that the checkout is current.\n43: \n44: When the operator passes `--json`, return the engine report as one JSON document and omit the prose dashboard and next steps.\n45: \n46: ```text\n47: Spec-kit Release Check\n48: \n49: Release position: [ahead|behind|at-release|unknown] [release tag or UNKNOWN]\n50: Upstream latest: [tag or UNKNOWN]\n51: Checkout: [head]  Ahead: [count]  Behind: [count]  Dirty: [yes|no]\n52: Report status: [status]\n53: \n54: Quiet units: [current count] current, [local count] local (no action)\n55: \n56: | Status | Unit | Kind | File changes | Changelog highlights |\n57: |--------|------|------|--------------|----------------------|\n58: | [update|new|customized|conflict|removed|blocked|downgrade|unknown] | [unit] | [kind] | [class counts] | [highlights or none found] |\n59: \n60: Next steps\n61: [action-specific next step]\n62: ```\n63: \n64: Files the engine classes `generated` (a leaf manifest, the trigger index and its sidecars, a compiled-route activation manifest, or a graph-metadata change inside its `derived` block) were rewritten by a generator. They never count as customizations. Include them in class counts and offer no decision.\n65: \n66: Show a row for each unit that is not `current` or `local`, grouped by status. Combine `current` and `local` into the quiet line and include both counts. Include counts for statuses with no matching unit as zero in the summary when the engine report provides status counts. Preserve an unexpected unit status visibly as `unknown`. Show available changelog highlights from the selected release and unit. If upstream latest is unavailable, display `UNKNOWN` and its engine error when present.\n67: \n68: ### Check next steps\n69: \n70: Use the applicable line or lines:\n71: \n72: ```text\n73: Customized or conflict units need decisions: /doctor:update align [same release and scope flags]\n74: Removed units need a decision review: /doctor:update align [same release and scope flags]\n75: Only update or new units need writes: /doctor:update apply [same release and scope flags]\n76: Removed, blocked or unknown units need review before applying: inspect the status details, then choose align or apply as appropriate.\n77: Downgrade units are older in the selected release than in this checkout. Apply never writes them. Roll back the apply that took the newer release, or use git, to return to an older release.\n78: Advisor graph rebuild after an update: /doctor:skill-advisor rebuild\n79: Shipped AGENTS.md sections after an update: /doctor:agents-md check\n80: No selected units need an update.\n81: ```\n82: \n83: When offering apply without a decisions file, add this note if no earlier alignment run is known:\n84: \n85: ```text\n86: No alignment run is needed for update and new units. /doctor:update apply plans from the current check, writes only those units, and re-checks each file against its base before writing. Customized or conflicting units are skipped until /doctor:update align records decisions for them.\n87: ```\n88: \n89: When the report's `baseRecording.needed` is true, add:\n90: \n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 91]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-update-presentation.txt\",