{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794534670146,"sessionID":"ses_e2d67e477ffeoyZimdgc817KZg","part":{"partID":"prt_1d299fc51001KgmDa5lEs7QNs1","sessionID":"ses_e2d67e477ffeoyZimdgc817KZg","messageID":"msg_1d299f34b001RecpZQ0VN5gSwO","type":"tool","id":"call_aba61af26b244033970bae41","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"sed -n '60,150p' .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-git-presentation.txt; echo '=== CI ==='; sed -n '38,110p' .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-ci-presentation.txt","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":"```\n\n### Cross-Target Flag Failure\n\n```text\nFlag '[flag]' is not valid for target '[target]'. Did you mean `/doctor:git [suggested-target] [flag]`?\nSTATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"cross_target_flag_injection\"\n```\n\n## 2. DASHBOARD / CHECKPOINT LAYOUT\n\n### Route Manifest Display\n\nRender this table for `list`, `?`, or `--list`. Values should mirror `_routes.yaml`.\n\n| Target | Workflow | Mutation Class | One-Line Purpose |\n|--------|----------|----------------|------------------|\n| `hooks` | `doctor-git-hooks.yaml` | mutates | List the shipped hook gates with their saved settings and switch one on or off in local or global git config |\n| `standards` | `doctor-git-standards.yaml` | mutates | Show the enforced commit, PR and branch rules and change them in the repository's own `.sk-git/` copies |\n| `setup` | `doctor-git-setup.yaml` | read-only | Run every sk-git check in its read-only form and name the repair for each failure |\n\n### Setup Dashboard\n\nRender this compact panel after setup and before YAML execution when target resolution or flags were non-trivial.\n\n```text\nDOCTOR ROUTE SETUP\nTarget: [target]\nWorkflow: .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/[yaml]\nMutation class: [the target's mutating value in _routes.yaml: mutates for hooks and standards, read-only for setup]\nExecution mode: INTERACTIVE\nSetup values: [key=value list]\nPresentation: .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-git-presentation.txt\nNext: load workflow YAML\n```\n\n### Hooks: Gate Table And Hand-Off\n\nRender the script's table as returned, then this block.\n\n```text\nHOOK INSTALL\n[the install status lines: hooksPath, and each hook as linked, SHADOWED or missing]\n\nSWITCHES THIS COMMAND DOES NOT SAVE\n   remotePush, massDeletion   per-push approvals: set SPECKIT_ALLOW_REMOTE_PUSH=1 or\n                              SPECKIT_ALLOW_MASS_DELETION=1 on that one git push only\n   commit-msg                 has no off switch; change or remove its rules with /doctor:git standards\n   Whole-hook kill switches   SYSTEM_GIT_COMMIT_HOOKS_DISABLED, SYSTEM_GIT_HOOKS_CHECK_DISABLED,\n                              SK_GIT_PREFLIGHT_DISABLED, SYSTEM_GIT_WORKTREE_GUARD_DISABLED:\n                              see and change them with /doctor:env\n```\n\nThen ask:\n\n```text\nWhich gate should change? Reply with the key and on or off, for example: cardSync off\nAdd \"global\" to change it for every repository on this machine; the default is this repository only.\nReply done to finish without a change.\n```\n\n### Hooks: Change Plan And Approval\n\n```text\nGATE CHANGE PLAN\nGate: [key] ([hook]) - [what it does]\nNow: [on|off] ([default|local config|global config])\nChange: [on|off] in [local|global] config\nWill run: [the git config command, or nothing to change]\nBypass for one run without saving: [ENV]=1 git [commit|push] ...\n```\n\nWith `--dry-run`, follow the plan with `Dry run: nothing was written.` and continue without asking.\n\nOtherwise ask:\n\n```text\nApply this change? Reply approve to write it, or no to cancel.\n```\n\n### Standards: Status\n\nRender the script's status as returned, then:\n\n```text\nWHERE THE RULES COME FROM\n   1. git config skgit.contractDir, when set\n   2. .sk-git/ at the repository root\n   3. the shipped sk-git templates (never edited by this command)\nActive: [source]\n```\n=== CI ===\n\nValid targets: report, scaffold, toggle\n\n## 3. DASHBOARD AND PLAN LAYOUT\n\n### Route Manifest Display\n\nRender this table for `menu`, `list` or `?`. Values should mirror `_routes.yaml`.\n\n| Target | Workflow | Mutation Class | One-Line Purpose |\n|--------|----------|----------------|------------------|\n| `report` | `doctor-ci-report.yaml` | read-only | List every workflow with its switch state, triggers, path filters, purpose and drift flags, and name the newest non-rebuild commit on the default branch |\n| `scaffold` | `doctor-ci-scaffold.yaml` | mutates | Create one new `.github/workflows/` file from the standards templates, after an explicit yes |\n| `toggle` | `doctor-ci-toggle.yaml` | mutates | Set or clear one switch variable from the repository CI profile, after an explicit yes |\n\n### Setup Dashboard\n\nRender this compact panel after target resolution and before YAML execution when the target or flags were non-trivial.\n\n```text\nDOCTOR ROUTE SETUP\nTarget: [target]\nWorkflow: .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/[yaml]\nMutation class: [the target's mutating value in _routes.yaml]\nExecution mode: INTERACTIVE\nSetup values: [key=value list]\nPresentation: .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-ci-presentation.txt\nNext: load workflow YAML\n```\n\n### Report Summary\n\nRender the script's table as returned, one row per workflow, under this header.\n\n```text\nCI WORKFLOW REPORT\nWorkflows: [n]  Jobs: [n]\nVariables: [none | NAME=state for each variable that is set | unknown (reason)]\nProfile: [default | repo | cli | git-config] ([the profile path, when there is one])[; ignored [path], written for [repository], this repository is [current or unknown]; shown only when the skill-folder profile names another repository]\nNewest non-rebuild SHA: [40 hex | none] ([reason])\n\n[table: Workflow | Switch | Jobs | Events | Filters | Drift flags | Purpose]\n\nNot checked: path-parity, shell-strict-mode, matrix-guidance. The workflow standards packet owns these rules, so a clean row is not a pass for them.\n```\n\nSwitch values: `on` (every job runs), `off` (every job is skipped by a variable set to off), `partial` (some jobs skip and some run), `missing` (no job carries a switch while the CI profile requires one) and `unknown` (gh could not be read). A variable is shown as `off`, `unset`, `other` or `unknown`, never by its value. The variables are the profile's declared switches, then any other name a workflow compares against `off`.\n\n### Scaffold Plan And Approval\n\n```text\nWORKFLOW SCAFFOLD PLAN\nTarget file: .github/workflows/[name].yml\nTemplates: .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-ci/assets/workflow-template.yml, .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-ci/assets/job-block-template.yml\nSwitch group: [a group from the CI profile, here TESTS|REPORTS|REVIEW|FRESHNESS|MESSAGES | none]\nTimeout: [n] minutes\nREADME rows to add by hand: [one row per table the profile's workflowsReadme lists | none, the profile names no README]\n\n--- proposed file ---\n[the whole file]\n--- end of file ---\n\nWrite this file? [yes/no]\n```\n\nWith `--dry-run`, follow the plan with `Dry run: nothing was written.` and stop without asking.\n\nA refused name prints one of these lines, `STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"refused\"` and exits without a plan:\n\n```text\nREFUSE: the target path already exists; scaffold creates new workflows only\nREFUSE: [name] is a protected workflow\nREFUSE: [name] is not a bare lowercase hyphen-case name ending in .yml\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"```\n\n### Cross-Target Flag Failure\n\n```text\nFlag '[flag]' is not valid for target '[target]'. Did you mean `/doctor:git [suggested-target] [flag]`?\nSTATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"cross_target_flag_injection\"\n```\n\n## 2. DASHBOARD / CHECKPOINT LAYOUT\n\n### Route Manifest Display\n\nRender this table for `list`, `?`, or `--list`. Values should mirror `_routes.yaml`.\n\n| Target | Workflow | Mutation Class | One-Line Purpose |\n|--------|----------|----------------|------------------|\n| `hooks` | `doctor-git-hooks.yaml` | mutates | List the shipped hook gates with their saved settings and switch one on or off in local or global git config |\n| `standards` | `doctor-git-standards.yaml` | mutates | Show the enforced commit, PR and branch rules and change them in the repository's own `.sk-git/` copies |\n| `setup` | `doctor-git-setup.yaml` | read-only | Run every sk-git check in its read-only form and name the repair for each failure |\n\n### Setup Dashboard\n\nRender this compact panel after setup and before YAML execution when target resolution or flags were non-trivial.\n\n```text\nDOCTOR ROUTE SETUP\nTarget: [target]\nWorkflow: .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/[yaml]\nMutation class: [the target's mutating value in _routes.yaml: mutates for hooks and standards, read-only for setup]\nExecution mode: INTERACTIVE\nSetup values: [key=value list]\nPresentation: .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-git-presentation.txt\nNext: load workflow YAML\n```\n\n### Hooks: Gate Table And Hand-Off\n\nRender the script's table as returned, then this block.\n\n```text\nHOOK INSTALL\n[the install status lines: hooksPath, and each hook as linked, SHADOWED or missing]\n\nSWITCHES THIS COMMAND DOES NOT SAVE\n   remotePush, massDeletion   per-push approvals: set SPECKIT_ALLOW_REMOTE_PUSH=1 or\n                              SPECKIT_ALLOW_MASS_DELETION=1 on that one git push only\n   commit-msg                 has no off switch; change or remove its rules with /doctor:git standards\n   Whole-hook kill switches   SYSTEM_GIT_COMMIT_HOOKS_DISABLED, SYSTEM_GIT_HOOKS_CHECK_DISABLED,\n                              SK_GIT_PREFLIGHT_DISABLED, SYSTEM_GIT_WORKTREE_GUARD_DISABLED:\n                              see and change them with /doctor:env\n```\n\nThen ask:\n\n```text\nWhich gate should change? Reply with the key and on or off, for example: cardSync off\nAdd \"global\" to change it for every repository on this machine; the default is this repository only.\nReply done to finish without a change.\n```\n\n### Hooks: Change Plan And Approval\n\n```text\nGATE CHANGE PLAN\nGate: [key] ([hook]) - [what it does]\nNow: [on|off] ([default|local config|global config])\nChange: [on|off] in [local|global] config\nWill run: [the git config command, or nothing to change]\nBypass for one run without saving: [ENV]=1 git [commit|push] ...\n```\n\nWith `--dry-run`, follow the plan with `Dry run: nothing was written.` and continue without asking.\n\nOtherwise ask:\n\n```text\nApply this change? Reply approve to write it, or no to cancel.\n```\n\n### Standards: Status\n\nRender the script's status as returned, then:\n\n```text\nWHERE THE RULES COME FROM\n   1. git config skgit.contractDir, when set\n   2. .sk-git/ at the repository root\n   3. the shipped sk-git templates (never edited by this command)\nActive: [source]\n```\n=== CI ===\n\nValid targets: report, scaffold, toggle\n\n## 3. DASHBOARD AND PLAN LAYOUT\n\n### Route Manifest Display\n\nRender this table for `menu`, `list` or `?`. Values should mirror `_routes.yaml`.\n\n| Target | Workflow | Mutation Class | One-Line Purpose |\n|--------|----------|----------------|------------------|\n| `report` | `doctor-ci-report.yaml` | read-only | List every workflow with its switch state, triggers, path filters, purpose and drift flags, and name the newest non-rebuild commit on the default branch |\n| `scaffold` | `doctor-ci-scaffold.yaml` | mutates | Create one new `.github/workflows/` file from the standards templates, after an explicit yes |\n| `toggle` | `doctor-ci-toggle.yaml` | mutates | Set or clear one switch variable from the repository CI profile, after an explicit yes |\n\n### Setup Dashboard\n\nRender this compact panel after target resolution and before YAML execution when the target or flags were non-trivial.\n\n```text\nDOCTOR ROUTE SETUP\nTarget: [target]\nWorkflow: .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/[yaml]\nMutation class: [the target's mutating value in _routes.yaml]\nExecution mode: INTERACTIVE\nSetup values: [key=value list]\nPresentation: .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-ci-presentation.txt\nNext: load workflow YAML\n```\n\n### Report Summary\n\nRender the script's table as returned, one row per workflow, under this header.\n\n```text\nCI WORKFLOW REPORT\nWorkflows: [n]  Jobs: [n]\nVariables: [none | NAME=state for each variable that is set | unknown (reason)]\nProfile: [default | repo | cli | git-config] ([the profile path, when there is one])[; ignored [path], written for [repository], this repository is [current or unknown]; shown only when the skill-folder profile names another repository]\nNewest non-rebuild SHA: [40 hex | none] ([reason])\n\n[table: Workflow | Switch | Jobs | Events | Filters | Drift flags | Purpose]\n\nNot checked: path-parity, shell-strict-mode, matrix-guidance. The workflow standards packet owns these rules, so a clean row is not a pass for them.\n```\n\nSwitch values: `on` (every job runs), `off` (every job is skipped by a variable set to off), `partial` (some jobs skip and some run), `missing` (no job carries a switch while the CI profile requires one) and `unknown` (gh could not be read). A variable is shown as `off`, `unset`, `other` or `unknown`, never by its value. The variables are the profile's declared switches, then any other name a workflow compares against `off`.\n\n### Scaffold Plan And Approval\n\n```text\nWORKFLOW SCAFFOLD PLAN\nTarget file: .github/workflows/[name].yml\nTemplates: .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-ci/assets/workflow-template.yml, .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-ci/assets/job-block-template.yml\nSwitch group: [a group from the CI profile, here TESTS|REPORTS|REVIEW|FRESHNESS|MESSAGES | none]\nTimeout: [n] minutes\nREADME rows to add by hand: [one row per table the profile's workflowsReadme lists | none, the profile names no README]\n\n--- proposed file ---\n[the whole file]\n--- end of file ---\n\nWrite this file? [yes/no]\n```\n\nWith `--dry-run`, follow the plan with `Dry run: nothing was written.` and stop without asking.\n\nA refused name prints one of these lines, `STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"refused\"` and exits without a plan:\n\n```text\nREFUSE: the target path already exists; scaffold creates new workflows only\nREFUSE: [name] is a protected workflow\nREFUSE: [name] is not a bare lowercase hyphen-case name ending in .yml\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"sed -n '60,150p' .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-git-presentation.txt; echo '=== CI ==='; sed -n '38,110p' .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-ci-presentation.txt\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"}"},"time":{"start":1794534669393,"end":1794534670146}}}}
