{"type":"text","timestamp":1794534813852,"sessionID":"ses_e2d67e477ffeoyZimdgc817KZg","part":{"id":"prt_1d29c12270028PCuZidtirPJZp","sessionID":"ses_e2d67e477ffeoyZimdgc817KZg","messageID":"msg_1d29bdd02001nP8cLdOYQbp7Th","type":"text","text":"T015 complete.\n\n**File written**\n\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-presentation.txt` (+93 lines, only file changed)\n\nAdded a new section `## 8. Embedder Setup Presentation` with:\n\n- `### Probe Dashboard` — binary, server version, model tag and size, daemon, active embedder, command vector coverage and lane state, with unread values kept unread\n- `### Plan Table` — `| Step | Cost | Undo |` rows for the printed Ollama install, the background server start, the model pull and `skill_graph_scan`\n- `### Approval Prompt` — names the steps, the database `skill_graph_scan` writes and what never runs, with the `STATUS=CANCELLED ACTION=cancelled` result on anything but approve\n- `### Dry-Run Result` — probe and plan, then `Dry run: nothing was pulled, started or written.` and `STATUS=OK`\n- `### Final Result` — server, model, coverage, lane state, next action (daemon restart when the active embedder is null) and the OK/FAIL rule\n\n**Verify output**\n\n```\n$ rg -n -i \"embedder\" .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-presentation.txt\n203:## 8. Embedder Setup Presentation\n205:Render these blocks for `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder`. The probe runs first and changes nothing. Every value is printed as the probe or the cost script returned it, and an unread value stays unread.\n212:EMBEDDER SETUP PROBE\n217:Active embedder: [<backend> <model>|none|unread, the daemon is absent]\n222:A missing binary, an absent server and a missing model are findings, not failures of the route. An exit 75 from `advisor_status` means the daemon is absent, so the active embedder, the command vectors and the lane state stay `unread`.\n226:Render one row per missing step, in dependency order. A step the probe found present is not listed and is not run. Each cost comes from `measure-embedder-cost.mjs` or, when the cost script cannot run, from the install guide with a note that the live measurement was unavailable.\n229:EMBEDDER SETUP PLAN\n261:EMBEDDER SETUP CANCELLED\n263:Next: /doctor:skill-advisor embedder\n272:EMBEDDER SETUP DRY RUN\n285:EMBEDDER SETUP RESULT\n290:Next: [none|restart the advisor daemon, the active embedder is resolved at startup|the repair the failed check names]\n294:Report `STATUS=OK` only when the lane is enabled and the embedded count is above zero. Otherwise report `STATUS=FAIL` and name the check that did not pass. When the active embedder is null, name a daemon restart, then rerun the probe.\n```\n\n14 matching lines, at least five required. Code fences are balanced (34 fence lines). No em dash, semicolon, spec path, task id, ADR or REQ id in the added lines.\n\n**Not done**\n\n- Did not tick the checkbox in `tasks.md`.\n- Did not touch `_routes.yaml`, the startup menu, the route manifest display table or `skill-advisor.md`, since those are T014 and T018. That leaves the section 1 menu and section 2 table without an `embedder` entry, which is a gap in the task split for the orchestrator to note.","time":{"start":1794534806055,"end":1794534813852}}}
